= Coordination problem =

== Overview ==
'''Coordination problem''' is a strategic situation in which participants can benefit from matching, aligning, or otherwise making mutually compatible choices but may fail to select the same compatible outcome.

Coordination problems often have multiple acceptable equilibria. The difficulty is not necessarily conflicting interests; it can be uncertainty about what others will do, which convention will be used, or which equilibrium will be selected.

Examples include choosing a common technical standard, selecting which side of the road to drive on, meeting at the same location, or synchronizing actions across organizations.

Communication, conventions, focal points, repeated interaction, standards, leadership, and shared signals can reduce coordination failure.

== Boundaries ==
* coordination problem ≠ collective-action problem by identity
* multiple equilibria ≠ conflict of interest
* coordination ≠ centralized control

